    <string name="setup_refused_body">Termux refused the command.\n\nCause: %1$s\n\nCheck in Termux: allow-external-apps = true in ~/.termux/termux.properties, then termux-reload-settings.\nAlso check the RUN_COMMAND permission in the app settings.</string>
    <string name="no_response_body">No response after 5 minutes.\n\nIf this is the first launch the download can be slow. Otherwise check in Termux:\n• allow-external-apps = true\n• log: ~/.cyberstrike-setup.log</string>
    <string name="termux_required_body">CyberStrike runs inside Termux.\n\n1. Tap «Download and install»: the app downloads the right APK from GitHub releases and opens the installer (you must allow unknown sources).\n2. Open Termux once and enable execution from other apps:\n   ~/.termux/termux.properties → allow-external-apps = true\n   then run: termux-reload-settings\n\n3. Come back here: it retries by itself.\n\nAlternatively you can use a remote CyberStrike server: ⋮ → Settings → Server URL.</string>
